    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on this August 10th slate, the focus remains firmly on capitalizing on stolen base potential and high-leverage order positioning. **Tyler Soderstrom** (74.75) and **Corbin Carroll** (73.48) represent our strongest plays of the day. **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits immensely from a favorable park factor and a matchup against Freddy Peralta, while **Corbin Carroll** continues to be our primary engine for SB production, carrying a massive floor given his #2 spot in the order against Gabriel Hughes. **Mickey Moniak** (61.43) and **Henry Bolte** (61.02) also grade out as strong starts, with **Mickey Moniak** receiving a significant +14% boost due to a prime platoon advantage against Michael Soroka, and **Henry Bolte** leveraging an elite #1 order slot to maximize his exposure in a hitter-friendly environment.\n\nThe most difficult decision today centered on **Austin Riley** (48.94), who sits at the bottom of our active recommendations. While his raw power remains a threat, a marginal score\u2014compounded by a 31% rain risk\u2014makes him the most volatile piece of our lineup. He narrowly avoided the bench in favor of **Max Muncy** (54.98); although **Max Muncy** is buried in the #8 hole, his park factor advantage against Freddy Peralta provides just enough cushion over **Austin Riley** to justify the start. We are currently navigating a depleted bench as **James Wood** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** remain sidelined on the IL, while **Josh Naylor** and **Jose Caballero** are unavailable due to team off-days. With **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Cole Young**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** all currently relegated to bench or reserve roles, we will monitor potential late-lineup shifts for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Brice Turang** to ensure we aren't leaving any efficiency on the table.",
